# Project context

Weather-Aware Truck Routing: React + Django app recommending the safest of 3 truck routes based on weather at each checkpoint's ETA, load weight, and travel time. Graded assessment — **correctness and clarity over extra features.**

## Source of truth (read when relevant)

1. `fs-assessment-spotter.pdf` — original requirements
2. `AGENTS.md` — locked decisions + interpretations of ambiguous rules
3. `PROGRESS.md` — built vs remaining
4. `.cursor/rules/*` — guardrails

## Grading weights (use them to break ties)

- 40% routes, weather, risk & recommendation logic → correctness, tests
- 40% UI, map & heatmap smoothness/performance → WebGL, no refetch on slider
- 15% code quality → small focused modules, clean boundaries
- 5% docs & walkthrough → README states every assumption

## In scope

Origin/destination/departure/load form · 3 HERE truck routes · checkpoints at 10/25/50 mi · weather at ETA · risk + load rules · ranked recommendation · map with routes, checkpoints, risk, ETAs, summaries · corridor heatmap with 0–48 h slider · hosting · README.

## Out of scope (do not build unless asked)

Auth/accounts, persistence of trips, own routing engine, live traffic, hours-of-service/rest stops, notifications, mobile app, i18n.

Do not invent product behavior. Ambiguity → add a line to `AGENTS.md` "Interpretations" and a test, or ask.
